theory_blocks.body:
Join two pairs of corresponding points (object vertex to image vertex) and draw the **perpendicular bisector** of each segment;

the two bisectors meet at the centre of rotation, because every point on a perpendicular bisector is equally distant from both ends of that segment, and the centre must be equidistant from a point and its image.

Tracing paper also works: hold a pencil point at a trial centre and turn the paper until the shape fits exactly onto its image.

